---
import Scene from "@openducktor/product-scenes/astro";
import { links } from "../content/site";
import FeatureTile from "../ui/FeatureTile.astro";
import SectionHead from "../ui/SectionHead.astro";
import "./Features.css";
---

<section id="features" class="section features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <SectionHead eyebrow="Features" id="features-title">
      <Fragment slot="title"
        >Plan in a session, control every prompt, and run your commands in the worktree.</Fragment
      >
      <p>
        Sessions and the MCP server use the same local task store as the board. A task that an agent
        creates in a session or through MCP shows on the board at once.
      </p>
    </SectionHead>
    <div class="features-grid">
      <FeatureTile
        id="feature-chat"
        label="Sessions"
        title="Plan a feature in a session, and get tasks on the board."
        size="full"
      >
        A session can work outside a task. Give it a custom role and a reusable prompt. The agent
        searches your tasks and creates the missing ones. Open a new task from the session, and
        start its Builder without leaving the session.
        <Scene name="chat" slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
      <FeatureTile
        id="feature-mcp"
        label="MCP"
        title="Use your tasks from any MCP client."
        size="half"
      >
        Add <a class="text-link" href={links.mcp}><code>@openducktor/mcp</code></a> to another agent.
        It can search, read, create, and update your tasks. It sends each call to the running app, so
        the board shows a new task at once.
        <Scene name="mcp" slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
      <FeatureTile
        id="feature-prompts"
        label="Prompts"
        title="Read and replace every built-in prompt."
        size="half"
      >
        The settings show each built-in prompt that OpenDucktor sends to an agent. Replace a prompt
        for all repositories or for one repository. OpenDucktor checks the placeholders of each
        active override, and it does not save until they are valid.
        <Scene name="prompts" slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
      <FeatureTile
        id="feature-actions"
        label="Actions"
        title="Run your project commands in the task worktree."
        size="full"
      >
        An action is a named command of the repository, such as your dev server or your tests. Run
        it from the top bar of a session: each run opens a new terminal in the worktree of the task,
        or in the folder of a session without a task. An action can also run when OpenDucktor
        creates a worktree, and the agent can wait until it finishes.
        <Scene name="actions" slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
